From 8f3d1a958cdcc25a066cc841a350bb47e15ee77c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sai Kruthi Wusirika <kruthiwusirika@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:20:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(operator): support RTX PRO 6000 Server and GB300 in DGDR
 GPU discovery

AIConfigurator has shipped system definitions for rtx_pro_6000_server
and gb300 since v0.8.0, but the DGDR gpuSku enum did not accept either
name and InferHardwareSystem had no rule for the products, so clusters
with these GPUs could not use hardware auto-discovery at all. Issue
#13239 reports this for the RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition and a
follow-up comment reproduces it for GB300.

Add both values to the GPUSKUType enum and map the product names the
GPU Feature Discovery labels and DCGM report: "NVIDIA GB300" and
"NVIDIA-GB300" infer gb300, and "NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server
Edition" and its label form infer rtx_pro_6000_server. The RTX rule
requires the Server marker because the Workstation and Max-Q editions
have no profiler data; they stay unrecognized rather than silently
profiling against the server card's numbers. GB300 is placed ahead of
the B300 rule, which already refuses to match it.

Regenerate the CRD, the Python DGDR types, and the API reference docs;
add inference, enrichment, and admission test cases; and document the
new product mappings in the DGDR reference page.

Relates to #13239

Signed-off-by: Sai Kruthi Wusirika <kruthiwusirika@gmail.com>
